---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import FeatureRow from "../../components/FeatureRow.astro";
import Shot from "../../components/Shot.astro";
import SubNav from "../../components/SubNav.astro";
import { ACTIVITIES_PAGES } from "../../sections";
---

<Base og="activities"
  title="Climbing"
  description="Climbing in Heracles Records: your hardest send, a grade pyramid, grade over time and every session climb by climb, in the scale you chose in COROS."
>
  <SubNav pages={ACTIVITIES_PAGES} label="Activities" />

  <section class="wrap page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Climbing</p>
    <h1>Grade by grade.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Indoor routes, bouldering, outdoor days and multi-pitch, read the way a climber counts
      them: in climbs rather than kilometres, in grades rather than pace, and in what you sent
      and how.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section-tight">
    <Shot name="36-climbing" alt="Climbing: this week in climbs, the hardest send, the share sent, the onsight grade and weekly volume by kind" eager />
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="feature-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">The screen</p>
      <h2>A climber's numbers, not a runner's.</h2>
      <ul class="ticks columns">
        <li><strong>This week in climbs</strong>, routes and problems, sent or not, against the weeks before.</li>
        <li><strong>Your hardest send</strong> of the last 12 weeks, a route's and a boulder's, with how and when you sent it.</li>
        <li><strong>The share you sent</strong> of the climbs you marked over four weeks, routes and problems apart.</li>
        <li><strong>Your onsight grade</strong> as set in the COROS app, and how many sends you made above it.</li>
        <li><strong>Weekly volume</strong> in climbs, climbing time or sessions, by kind, with a four-week average.</li>
        <li><strong>Time on the wall</strong>: how much of a session is spent climbing, the average route and problem, and falls a climb.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <FeatureRow shot="38-climb-grades" alt="A grade pyramid of sends and attempts beside the average send over the weeks, with the onsight grade marked">
      <p class="eyebrow">Grades</p>
      <h2>A pyramid of what you sent.</h2>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><strong>A row for every grade</strong>: sent first go, sent after working it, or tried, with your onsight grade marked.</li>
        <li><strong>Grade over time</strong>: your average send and the hardest send of each week.</li>
        <li><strong>One scale</strong>: every grade in the one you chose in COROS's climb settings, a grade logged in another converted through COROS's own table.</li>
        <li><strong>Routes and boulders apart</strong>: a V5 is never set against a 6b. Aid, ice and mixed grades are named but not ranked.</li>
      </ul>
    </FeatureRow>

    <FeatureRow shot="37-climb" alt="A climbing session: each climb as a block where it was climbed, by grade, above the session's heart rate" flip>
      <p class="eyebrow">A session's page</p>
      <h2>Every climb, in the order climbed.</h2>
      <p>
        Each climb is a block placed where it fell in the session and as wide as its time on the
        wall, by grade, time on the wall or height, with the falls on it and the attempts drawn
        open. Below, the heart rate on the same clock, then the climbs one by one: the grade,
        how it went, the time on the wall and the rest after. An outdoor day gathers its pitches
        into routes.
      </p>
    </FeatureRow>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title">What you mark is what is counted.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Your watch keeps a climb as a lap, from the foot of the route to its top, with the grade
        and how it went if you mark them. A climb left unmarked still counts as climbed, but in
        neither your sends nor your attempts, and one without a grade stays out of the pyramid.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
